Patent abstract
text
A system and method for autonomous agent treasuries is provided. The system receives an agent-initiated financial action request, evaluates the request against a treasury policy, determines reserve availability, applies spend limits, determines whether human approval is required, dispatches the action using an idempotency key, generates a receipt, reconciles the completed effect and generates an evidence record. The system distinguishes reversible local actions from irreversible external effects and applies different controls to each. The system may revoke agent authority, preserve evidence and initiate recovery.
Core inventive mechanism
text
Agent Action Request   → Treasury Policy   → Reserve Check   → Spend Limit Check   → Approval Decision   → Idempotent Dispatch   → Receipt   → Effect Reconciliation   → Evidence Record   → Recovery
Key claims
text
1. A computer-implemented method for autonomous agent treasuries, comprising:    a. receiving an agent-initiated financial action request;    b. evaluating the request against a treasury policy;    c. determining reserve availability;    d. applying one or more spend limits;    e. determining whether human approval is required;    f. dispatching the action using an idempotency key;    g. generating a receipt;    h. reconciling the completed effect; and    i. generating an evidence record.  2. The method of claim 1, wherein the treasury policy distinguishes reversible local actions from irreversible external effects.  3. The method of claim 1, wherein the reserve availability includes an operating reserve, emergency reserve, vendor-payment reserve, investment reserve, compliance reserve or recovery reserve.  4. The method of claim 1, wherein the spend limit includes a daily, weekly, monthly, per-counterparty, per-category or per-action limit.  5. The method of claim 1, wherein the idempotency key prevents duplicate effects.  6. The method of claim 1, wherein the evidence record includes a hash of the request, policy decision, approval decision, receipt and reconciliation result.  7. The method of claim 1, further comprising revoking agent authority and initiating recovery.
