# AgentAssure Commons: A Shared Assurance Layer for Trustworthy AI Agents in Small Organizations  ## Abstract  Small organizations increasingly want to use AI agents for intake, research, scheduling, procurement, donor communications and case management. But they lack the security teams, compliance capacity and technical expertise needed to determine whether an agent is safe.  This paper proposes AgentAssure Commons, an open, community-governed assurance layer for organizations deploying AI agents. The system provides a capability inventory, policy templates, a tamper-evident evidence ledger, an audit dashboard, an adversarial test suite and recovery playbooks.  The paper argues that agent safety requires an execution boundary, not merely a prompt filter. It distinguishes reversible local actions from irreversible external effects and applies different controls to each.  ## Keywords  Agent assurance, AI agents, small organizations, security, audit, evidence ledger, policy templates, adversarial testing, recovery, governance  ## JEL Classification  L31, L86, O33  ## 1. Introduction  AI agents are increasingly used by small organizations.  ## 2. Problem statement  Small organizations lack the security teams, compliance capacity and technical expertise needed to determine whether an agent is safe.  ## 3. AgentAssure Commons  AgentAssure Commons provides a capability inventory, policy templates, a tamper-evident evidence ledger, an audit dashboard, an adversarial test suite and recovery playbooks.  ## 4. Capability inventory  A capability inventory defines what an agent can access and do.  ## 5. Policy templates  Policy templates define controls for privacy, financial authority, external communications and irreversible actions.  ## 6. Evidence ledger  A tamper-evident evidence ledger records agent actions, authorizations, approvals and outcomes.  ## 7. Adversarial test suite  An adversarial test suite tests prompt injection, data exfiltration, privilege escalation and unauthorized external effects.  ## 8. Audit dashboard  An audit dashboard lets non-technical administrators inspect agent actions.  ## 9. Recovery playbook  A recovery playbook defines suspension, revocation, incident response and service continuity.  ## 10. Governance  Community governance ensures that the system remains open, inspectable and resilient.  ## 11. Conclusion  AgentAssure Commons provides a shared assurance layer for trustworthy AI agents in small organizations.





















